   "id": "M1:T123",
   "speaker": "EndUser",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Software below the IOC level. There is likely to be software below the IOC level, but it should not require downloading, except possibly for upgrades, typically being placed into ROM or FLASH memory. Any access to this embedded software while it is connected to the system is strictly through software in the IOC. From outside the IOC this software appears as part of the electronics. Although this software is not considered part of the Gemini software, it is obviously an advantage (for maintenance purposes) to have it conform to the requirements of Gemini software.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
